tion_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:ae168f553524f5efa8800932a1d3e60edf2fd26d6761b050a0951f9b32ff3cbf","file":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":80,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5b330b98cf4f74cfb42d452969c686f59a44ec2c0acf0a76a3c2746d6e2dc65b","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:ae168f553524f5efa8800932a1d3e60edf2fd26d6761b050a0951f9b32ff3cbf","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Nonuniqueness-of-percolation-on-nonamenable-quasi-transitive-graphs-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L80"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:cayley}\nLet $\\Lambda$ be a nonamenable finitely generated group, and let $S$\nbe any finite symmetric generating set with the identity removed.\nFor Bernoulli bond percolation on the simple undirected Cayley graph\nwith edges $\\{x,xs\\}$, $x\\in\\Lambda$, $s\\in S$, the critical connection\noperator is bounded on counting-measure $\\ell^2(\\Lambda)$ and\n\\[\n \\pc<\\ptwo\\le\\pu.\n\\]\nThe simultaneous nonuniqueness interval in \\cref{thm:main} exists for\nevery such fixed generating set. At every fixed $p\\in(\\pc,\\pu)$,\nthere are almost surely infinitely many infinite open clusters."}
